From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:10:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8015: Add the SMC GPIO controller

The T8015 SMC exposes the PMU GPIOs through SMC keys (gPxx), as on the
other SoCs that use the apple,t8103-smc protocol, but the SMC node has no
apple,smc-gpio child. Add it, so boards can refer to these lines; the
iPhone X powers its Wi-Fi module from one of them.

[Orchard: moved from the t8015-x Wi-Fi power patch to the SoC file]
Signed-off-by: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
index 0cf1942..155adba 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8015.dtsi
@@ -616,6 +616,12 @@
 			mboxes = <&smc_mbox>;
 			power-domains = <&ps_smc_cpu>;
 
+			smc_gpio: gpio {
+				compatible = "apple,smc-gpio";
+				gpio-controller;
+				#gpio-cells = <2>;
+			};
+
 			smc_hwmon: hwmon {
 				compatible = "apple,smc-hwmon";
 			};
